# Copy to `apps/web/.env.local` (gitignored) to override the defaults below.
# All are optional — they default to localhost for normal dev.

# ── HTTP API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Origin of the HTTP API, used by the `/api/:path*` rewrite in next.config.ts.
#
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — deliberately NOT `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. The browser always calls
# `/api` on its OWN origin and Next proxies from there, so this value is never
# inlined into the CLIENT bundle and the API's real address is never exposed.
#
# BUT IT IS STILL A BUILD-TIME VALUE: changing it is a REBUILD (a REDEPLOY on
# Vercel), not a restart. Next evaluates rewrites() during `next build` and
# freezes the result into .next/routes-manifest.json; the running server reads
# that manifest and never re-reads next.config.ts. Verified by running an image
# built against http://api:3001 with a bogus API_ORIGIN — it still proxied to
# http://api:3001. "Not NEXT_PUBLIC_" and "runtime-configurable" are two
# different things, and only the first is true here.
#
# This proxy is not a convenience. `SameSite=Lax` cookies are not sent — and, as
# measured, not even STORED — cross-site, so with web and api on different
# origins the session cookie never sticks and every authenticated request 401s.
# Same-origin makes it a first-party cookie again. Dev uses the same path on
# purpose; a dev-only direct connection is what hid this bug.
# API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001

# ── Realtime gateway ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebSocket URL (apps/realtime). Default: ws://localhost:3002
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the BROWSER opens this socket directly: it is not proxied
# (a rewrite cannot proxy a WebSocket), so this must be an address the browser
# can reach. Inlined at build time, so changing it is a rebuild. In Docker
# Compose that means ws://localhost:3002 — a service name like ws://realtime:3002
# compiles fine and then fails in the browser. Use wss:// in production.
#
# The socket does NOT use the session cookie. Since Phase 4.3b (shipped) it
# authenticates with a single-use ticket from POST /auth/ws-ticket, passed via
# Sec-WebSocket-Protocol and verified at the upgrade behind an Origin allowlist.
# There is deliberately no cookie fallback.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=ws://localhost:3002

# ── Testing from a phone / another device on your LAN ───────────────────────
# Only the WEB origin needs to change: HTTP now flows through the web origin's
# /api proxy, so the api does NOT need to be reachable from the phone directly.
#
#   1. Start Next bound to all interfaces:
#        pnpm --filter @sketchsync/web dev -- -H 0.0.0.0
#   2. Open http://192.168.1.42:3000 on the phone (use your own IP).
#   3. Point the socket at the same host, since it is not proxied:
#        NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=ws://192.168.1.42:3002
#
# `API_ORIGIN` can stay http://localhost:3001 — the Next server resolves it
# server-side, not from the phone.
#
# The auth cookie is host-scoped, so the web origin and the realtime host must
# share a host; don't mix localhost and the LAN IP.
#
# WEB_ORIGIN in apps/api/.env is now defence-in-depth only (browser traffic is
# same-origin and no longer exercises CORS), but keep it accurate.
